    "text": "A dilute solution of sulphuric acid is electrolysed using a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> hours to produce hydrogen and oxygen gas. The total volume of gases produced at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>STP</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. (Nearest integer) [Given : Faraday constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>STP</mi></math>, molar volume of an ideal gas is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]",
